WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.370
Same question, two ways.

2
00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.370
«T'as pas vu mon portable ?» And:

3
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.440
«N'auriez-vous pas vu mon
téléphone ?» Both ask if

4
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.410
someone has seen your phone.

5
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.060
One belongs with friends.

6
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.000
The other is French at its most formal.

7
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
And French slang can
flip words inside out:

8
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.420
«relou» is «lourd», back to front.

9
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.750
So can a sentence with perfect
grammar still go wrong,

10
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.730
just because you chose «tu» or «vous»?

11
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.270
In this mission, you'll set the
points on a two-track railway,

12
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.480
and see where each choice leads.

13
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.230
Then you'll turn «Salut,
t'as reçu mon CV ?»

14
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.320
into an email to a company.

15
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: find out
what one small word can do.
